  "preserved_policies": [
    "First history page: chats are stored in <channel>_messages.json but are not counted in counter.csv. Only pages 2..n are passed to the chat counter as from_messages observations.",
    "Every observation on every counted page increments counter, including the requested channel itself and repeated chats.",
    "A newly observed public chat is enriched with GetFullChannelRequest; each linked chat in that response gets another GetFullChannelRequest for participants_count and is counted as channel_request with channel_req_targeted_by = the parent username. Its source list is not extended on later linked observations.",
    "Chats without a username key (basic groups) or with username None are not written, counted, or enriched.",
    "A ValueError from enrichment appends 'ID - <id>' to _exceptions-users-not-found.txt; the chat stays counted and in chats.txt.",
    "chats.txt and collected_chats.csv append across runs; counter.csv describes the current invocation; collected_chats.csv is merged with the current counter on id (left join).",
    "collected_chats.csv keeps one row per enrichment, so a chat enriched from two sources appears twice.",
    "Channel JSON and messages JSON are replaced on each run; JSON uses ensure_ascii=False, compact separators, and str() for datetime/bytes.",
    "History requests use limit=100, max_id=0, add_offset=0, offset_date=0, hash=0, min_id=<--min-id or 0>, offset_id=<min id of previous page>, stopping on the first empty page."
